Wait, they talk now? is MIT-licensed (LICENSE).

It runs on and is built against:
- Fabric Loader and Fabric API (FabricMC), Apache-2.0.
- Minecraft (Mojang): this mod adds no block, item, or entity of its own at this stage. The
  Modrinth listing icon (`docs/modrinth/icon.png`) is a render of vanilla's own villager head
  texture (`minecraft:villager`, `assets/minecraft/textures/entity/villager/villager.png`),
  composed onto the plain cubealgos navy badge (no grid -- this mod is not a Create Fly add-on)
  at build time by `tools/icon.py` from a local Minecraft client jar; no asset file is copied
  into this repo, only the rendered composite `icon.png` (`just icon`).

The 64 shipped villager voice lines are AI-generated audio (`docs/spec/operations/compliance.md`
`REL-REQ-004`): synthesized by Chatterbox (Resemble AI, github.com/resemble-ai/chatterbox, MIT code
+ MIT weights via huggingface.co/ResembleAI/chatterbox), a zero-shot voice-cloning TTS, conditioned
on a short reference clip of a public-domain human voice reading aloud — never on any Mojang audio
(`docs/spec/domains/audio.md` `AUDIO-DEC-006`). The reference reader: **Greg Giordano**, from his
LibriVox recording of Fyodor Dostoyevsky's *Short Stories* (librivox.org), a public-domain
recording of a public-domain text; the reference clip itself is never bundled, committed, or
redistributed, only read at generation time and discarded (`docs/spec/domains/audio.md` §3
"Reference", `COMP-REQ-002`). Chatterbox is a build-time tool only, never invoked, bundled, or
reachable at runtime (`AUDIO-REQ-005`). Piper TTS (github.com/rhasspy/piper, archived, MIT — the
frozen snapshot, not the actively maintained GPL-3.0 `OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl` fork) remains the
pipeline's fallback engine, unused by the shipped batch; its candidate voice models
(`en_US-joe-medium`, `en_US-kristin-medium`, `en_US-norman-medium`, all CC0 or public domain) are
recorded in `tools/voices/VOICES.md` in case it's ever needed again.

The alpha's near-silent placeholder audio (`AUDIO-REQ-002`) is fully replaced by this batch — no
placeholder ships from this release onward. NeoForge's own credit is added once its module lands
and its licence is verified (`docs/spec/operations/compliance.md`).

All shipped line text is original to this project, never third-party content
(`docs/spec/decisions/DEC-003-licence.md`); the shipped audio is a new synthesis conditioned on a
public-domain human voice reading a public-domain text, not a copy or reuse of any third-party
recording.
